// Galata Tower and the rooftops of Istanbul at sunset, with a portal torn open in the sky. The arena is 800 px wide,
// twice what it was, and the camera zooms to follow the fighters.
// The background (near.png) is traced from a photo with `cargo run --bin trace_photo`; the portal and the floor tile
// come from `cargo run --bin gen_sprites`. Swap any image for your own art.
// Layers go back to front. parallax: 1 = fixed on screen, 0 = fixed in the world. y: height of the layer's centre.
// glow: true makes a layer pulse (the portal).
(
    name: "Galata Tower",
    sky: (0.92, 0.62, 0.55),
    pillar: (0.62, 0.72, 0.88),
    floor_a: (0.58, 0.52, 0.52),
    floor_b: (0.50, 0.45, 0.46),
    layers: [
        (image: "backgrounds/galata/near.png", parallax: 0.0, z: -8.0, y: 91.0),
        (image: "backgrounds/galata/portal.png", parallax: 0.0, z: -7.5, y: 91.0, glow: true),
    ],
    floor_tile: Some("backgrounds/galata/floor.png"),
)
